      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
